From f4d8b1e520e635f9ea94e45c1f9c0067eb4107c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Uthe <chris.uthe@openhomefoundation.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:58:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add an optional non-compliance observer to the server

SendspinServer takes a noncompliance_observer that is called with every
spec violation the server flags in a client, before the server tolerates it
or, with allow_noncompliant_clients=False, rejects the client. Until now a
violation reached only the log, so a tool that judges clients had to parse
log text to learn why one was rejected.

Each ObservedNoncompliance carries the reason as the server logs it, the
server clock time, the client id once the handshake names it, and the
connection number the frame observer uses, so a violation can be matched to
the frames that led to it. A lenient server reports every occurrence, though
it logs each reason once. Without an observer nothing changes. An observer
that raises is logged and never affects the connection.
